d by signal intensity time course curve</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">MATLAB, For PBF, MTT, PBV, Mean, SD, ANOVA, Fisher&#x02019;s PLSD test</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">PBF, PBV &#x00026; MTT showed significant differences between normal volunteers and patients with PH (<italic>P</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Nikolaou <italic>et al</italic>[<xref rid="B34" ref-type="bibr">34</xref>], 2005</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Prospective, qualitative </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">29</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">16 females (mean age 54 &#x000b1; 17 yr), 13 males (Mean age 57 &#x000b1; 15 yr) </td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pulmonary hypertension &#x00026; CTEPH differentiation by perfusion MRI and pulmonary angiography</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Turbo fast low angle shot gradient echo MRI sequence was performed by using generalized auto calibrating partially parallel technique or GRAPPA</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Student t test for significance, ROC using SPSS software</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">
